{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The foreigner.</b> Who sows and reaps and harvests — you may <b>exact</b> it from him." "<b>You shall release the hand of your brother.</b> But not one who hands over his documents to the court. From here they said: Hillel the Elder enacted the prosbol, for the repair of the world, for he saw that the people refrained from lending to one another and transgressed what is written in the Torah. And this is the essence of the prosbol: 'I hand over to you, so-and-so and so-and-so, the judges of such-and-such a place, every debt that I have, that I may collect it whenever I wish.' And the judges and the witnesses sign below, and then the Sabbatical year does not release his loan, for it is as though the court has already collected this one's debt, and we do not read concerning it 'he shall not exact.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:52.419794336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}